azards"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1355803-i20241120-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2805-8","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1355803-i20241120","date":"2024-11-20","original_code":"746.2805(8)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-03-03","finding":"Prohibited Punishments - Restrictive device for time out: Infants are being placed in a restrictive device as a form of discipline.","topic":"other","source_record_id":"1026630994","violation_type_title":"Prohibited Punishments - Restrictive device for time out (26 TAC §746.2805(8))","topic_label":"Other"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1355803-i20241120-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1355803-i20241120","date":"2024-11-20","original_code":"746.1201(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-03-03","finding":"AP Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Ensure No Child Abused, Neglected, or Exploited: During a DFPS investigation, there was sufficient evidence to support that a caregiver abused and neglected children in care.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026630984","violation_type_title":"AP Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Ensure No Child Abused, Neglected, or Exploited (26 TAC §746.1201(4))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1355803-i20241120-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3317","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1355803-i20241120","date":"2024-11-20","original_code":"746.3317","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-03-03","finding":"Food Service and Preparation Requirement - Safe and Sanitary: Video footage showed a caregiver spraying Lysol around themselves while shaking a bottle for an infant.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026630993","violation_type_title":"Food Service and Preparation Requirement - Safe and Sanitary (26 TAC §746.3317)","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1355803-i20241120-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-201-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1355803-i20241120","date":"2024-11-20","original_code":"746.201(2)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-03-03","finding":"Written Personnel Policies: A caregiver failed to follow the operations smoke free and drug free section the personnel policies.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026630981","violation_type_title":"Written Personnel Policies (26 TAC §746.201(2))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1355803-i20241120-v6","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1355803-i20241120","date":"2024-11-20","original_code":"746.1201(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-03-03","finding":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control: During a DFPS investigation, there was sufficient evidence to support that a caregiver dropped an empty bouncer seat on the ground next to two infants on the ground. The bouncer seat did not hit the infants, however the caregiver exhibited bad judgement when attempting to move it this way.    During a DFPS investigation, there was sufficient evidence to support that a caregiver did not demonstrate good judgement when the caregiver sprayed Lysol in the close proximity of infants.    During a DFPS investigation, there was sufficient evidence to support that a caregiver did not use good judgement when they used their sleeve to wipe an infant's nose twice. Additionally, the caregiver did not wash hands after doing so.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026630991","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control (26 TAC §746.1201(1))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1355803-i20241120-v7","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3703-c","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1355803-i20241120","date":"2024-11-20","original_code":"746.3703(c)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-03-03","finding":"Not Under the Influence of Alcohol or Controlled Substance: During a DPFS investigation, it was found that a caregiver was under the influence of THC while caring for infants. The caregiver did not have a prescription for the controlled substance.","topic":"other","source_record_id":"1026630998","violation_type_title":"Not Under the Influence of Alcohol or Controlled Substance (26 TAC §746.3703(c))","topic_label":"Other"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1355803-i20241120-v8","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1003-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1355803-i20241120","date":"2024-11-20","original_code":"746.1003(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-03-03","finding":"Director Responsibilities - Employees Supervised: During a DFPS investigation, there was sufficient evidence to support that the director was not appropriately supervising caregivers when a caregiver was observed on video walking out of a classroom leaving infants unsupervised multiple times.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026630986","violation_type_title":"Director Responsibilities - Employees Supervised (26 TAC §746.1003(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1355803-i20241120-v9","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3703-d","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1355803-i20241120","date":"2024-11-20","original_code":"746.3703(d)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-03-03","finding":"No Smoking or Use of Tobacco Including E-Cigarettes or Vaporizers: During a DPFS investigation, a caregiver admitted to smoking a THC vape pen in the infant classroom m